g among other things and one  particularly sweet moment during the  shoot shows just what close friends they  became after Cooper it filmed an  especially tough scene which was vital  for his character he walked up to  Jackson's pickup truck and opened the  door only to discover a bunch of roses  that Gaga had left for him there on the  passenger seat if you've seen the movie  you'll understand why Cooper was so  moved by Gaga's gesture as the scene he  just filmed was a heartbreaking one for  Jackson the soundtrack to his star is  born' is jam-packed with original songs  some of which were actually written  during the shoot for example lady gaga  wrote the  I don't know what love is when she felt  completely overcome with emotion after  filming the scene in the cop bar and she  even used her character Ally's on-screen  notebook to write down the lyrics right  there in the moment  she later finished off the song with  Lukas Nelson's son of country music star  Willie Nelson Lucas not only wrote and  produced many of the movies original  songs with Gagarin Cooper but he and his  bandmates from promise of the real also  doubled as Jackson Mane's band in the  movie  Lady Gaga really hates watching movies  where you can tell the act as a  lip-syncing so despite the fact that her  co-star Bradley Cooper had no real  experience as a singer or musician  before a star is born she convinced him  to record all their vocal performances  live on the day of filming rather than  simply lip-synching to pre-recorded  tracks as often happens in movie  musicals although first time director  Cooper found singing live terrifying he  says it allowed him to capture the truth  in each performance  many of the movie's musical moments were  filmed at real venues like Glastonbury  Festival so to avoid the crowd recording  their brand new songs and leaking them a  line ahead of the film's release the  sound crew deliberately turned off the  amplifiers so the audience couldn't hear  the music or vocals that added another  level of work for the movie sound team  as they had to capture each venues  acoustics and apply them later in  post-production to make the voices sound  like they would have done during a big  concert using such enormous real-life  performance spaces like LA's Greek  Theatre and the Shrine Auditorium meant  the production needed lots of people in  the audience to get the right visuals  energy and enthusiasm to make the  concert look and feel real but instead  of using thousands of extras the  filmmakers instead turned to Lady Gaga's  dedicated fanbase known as her little  monsters who were given the chance to  buy tickets for each of the venues worth  filming took place all the proceeds from  which went to Gaga's Born This Way  Foundation and as an extra thank you to  her fans at the end of a late night  filming Gaga gave an impromptu piano  performance of two of her hits  Bradley Cooper may have many years  experience acting on camera but when it  came to playing a seasoned singer and  musician performing live on stage he  realized he needed to dedicate plenty of  time to preparing for the musical  aspects of the part so he got himself a  vocal coach and spent five days a week  for six months  how to sing not just as himself was also  in character as Jackson mane  to give you an idea of the kind of  progress cooper made with his singing  when he first started he found himself  getting out of breath after just one  verse so he certainly came a long way  from that to performing so many songs  live on film cooper also took guitar and  piano lessons and worked pretty much  every night for 12 months with lucas  nelson who also shared his own insights  on performing and acting like a  professional musician but cooper didn't  just work on his singing voice he also  spent months working on his speaking  voice using a dialect coach to help him  develop the rich tambour he wanted the  Jackson Mane's voice it proved to be a  real challenge and ini